Stop waiting for ignoreFailure attributes after a per-repo grace.

nixbot finished a build only when every attribute had finished, so a
best-effort (ignoreFailure) attribute on a builder that went away mid-build
(a laptop asleep) held the build, its status, its effects and any merge
queue until the 3 h build timeout. With `optional_build_grace` in the
repository's nixbot.toml, once the eval has ended and only ignoreFailure
attributes remain, nixbot waits at most that many seconds, then stops them
through the per-attribute cancel and records them as ignored failures; the
build then finishes normally. An attribute finishing within the grace ends
the build as soon as it does. A build-level cancel stays cancelled.

